						<name>The Sect</name>
						<adjective>powerist</adjective>
						<memberName>Poweror</memberName>
						<leaderTitleMale>Divine Chief</leaderTitleMale>
						<leaderTitleFemale>Divine Chief</leaderTitleFemale>
						<description>On the cavernous shell-world Boccocarro, during the &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;Powerist Funeral&lt;/color&gt;, people would come to the &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;Great Image&lt;/color&gt; at the pantheon of &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;Tol'marox&lt;/color&gt; and pray with life in their hearts. A mine hypervisor passed a law forbidding Powerors from rising to the ruling classes of Boccocarro. A renowned surface scavenger named Oxosbi Chabiara brought the Powerors together, and even recruited some of the abyssal marines. Chabiara gathered the Powerors in a surface tunnel and taught them of &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;Tol'marox&lt;/color&gt;'s wisdom.</description>
						<descriptionTemplate>On the cavernous shell-world Boccocarro, during the %%ritual0_name%%, people would come to the %%altar0_name%% at the %%altarRoomLabel%% of %%deity0_name%% and pray with life in their hearts. A mine hypervisor passed a law forbidding %%memberNamePlural%% from rising to the ruling classes of Boccocarro. A renowned surface scavenger named Oxosbi Chabiara brought the %%memberNamePlural%% together, and even recruited some of the abyssal marines. Chabiara gathered the %%memberNamePlural%% in a surface tunnel and taught them of %%deity0_name%%'s wisdom.</descriptionTemplate>
						<culture>Corunan</culture>
						<iconDef>AbstractsA</iconDef>
