						<name>Chelisi Temple</name>
						<adjective>Hinisic</adjective>
						<memberName>Hinisite</memberName>
						<leaderTitleMale>Divine Chiller</leaderTitleMale>
						<leaderTitleFemale>Divine Chiller</leaderTitleFemale>
						<description>The God of Self &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;Hinis&lt;/color&gt; used a pathogen to strike the settlers of the arid world Chelis blind, forcing them to understand that sight is a barrier to divine knowledge. A group of sand-warriors arose under a terrible chief. They trapped the Hinisites in a single water center. A cactus gatherer named Glenn Quagmire was blessed by &lt;color=#D09B61FF&gt;Hinis&lt;/color&gt; and gained miraculous knowledge of the unique power of each and every Hinisite. He said to each one what they needed to become their best self. The chief's sand-warriors, armed with sand-arrows, raided the parch-town of the Hinisites. Glenn offered them a peace pipe, and the sand-warriors put down their weapons.</description>
						<descriptionTemplate>The %%deity0_type%% %%deity0_name%% used a pathogen to strike the settlers of the arid world Chelis blind, forcing them to understand that sight is a barrier to divine knowledge. A group of sand-warriors arose under a terrible chief. They trapped the %%memberNamePlural%% in a single water center. A cactus gatherer named Glenn Quagmire was blessed by %%deity0_name%% and gained miraculous knowledge of the unique power of each and every %%memberName%%. He said to each one what they needed to become their best self. The chief's sand-warriors, armed with sand-arrows, raided the parch-town of the %%memberNamePlural%%. Glenn offered them a peace pipe, and the sand-warriors put down their weapons.</descriptionTemplate>
